# SOMS Backend - Supabase Connection Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env or use .NET User Secrets:
#
# Using .NET User Secrets (Recommended for local dev):
#   dotnet user-secrets set "ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection" "Host=db.xyz.supabase.co;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD;SSL Mode=Require;"
#
# Direct Connection (Port 5432):
# ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection="Host=db.xyz.supabase.co;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD;SSL Mode=Require;"
#
# Session Pooler (IPv4 compatible, Port 5432 or 6543):
# ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection="Host=aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres.your-project-ref;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD;SSL Mode=Require;"
